Delivered behaviour:
- The portal's production project references are exactly TaxLogicEngine,
  CaseProcessing, Tenancy, and Persistence, and it references neither TaxCases,
  CaseReview, nor DocumentExtraction in the project file or in the compiled
  assembly's reference set.
- No EF Core, DbContext, DbSet, SqlConnection, System.Data, Sqlite, or Npgsql
  token appears in the portal project file. Persistence exposes one registration
  extension and the composition root calls it.
- ModuleRegistration.cs remains the only place any Add*/TryAdd* appears in
  portal source, and calls exactly one registration extension per contributing
  module alongside the three unchanged spec 010 singletons.
- PortalStartupGuards refuses to start when the connection string is absent
  (every environment) and, outside Development, when the transport does not
  require encryption or disables certificate validation, when the key-ring
  settings are missing or blank, when the key ring is not registered per B-6, or
  when the registered session store is not the durable one.
- B-6 is implemented in the container, not in configuration. Outside Development
  the built service provider must hold IDataProtectionProvider, a non-null
  KeyManagementOptions.XmlRepository, and a non-null
  KeyManagementOptions.XmlEncryptor, and neither the repository nor the encryptor
  may be declared in the ASP.NET Core Data Protection framework assembly. That
  single assembly comparison rejects EphemeralXmlRepository,
  FileSystemXmlRepository, ReadOnlyFileSystemXmlRepository,
  RegistryXmlRepository, NullXmlEncryptor, InvalidEncryptor, DpapiXmlEncryptor,
  DpapiNGXmlEncryptor, CertificateXmlEncryptor, and the framework's default local
  fallback, while admitting the intended Azure Blob Storage repository protected
  by Azure Key Vault. Configuration values alone do not satisfy the guard.
- The null-repository case is treated as a refusal on measured grounds: a bare
  ASP.NET Core 8 host registers no IDataProtectionProvider at all, and even after
  AddDataProtection() the XmlRepository stays null while the key manager resolves
  a machine-local directory plus DPAPI lazily.
- Every message is a fixed, non-interpolated constant that echoes no configured
  value.
- The environment test is an ordinal comparison against
  Environments.Development. The IsDevelopment token appears exactly once in
  portal production source, guarding development fixture seeding, which is proved
  never invoked outside Development.
- Container validation stays unconditional, proved structurally rather than by
  the absence of a token.
- .gitignore excludes the developer Data Protection key ring.
- No EnsureCreated, Migrate, schema mutation, timer, hosted service, or
  scheduler was added.

B-6 host-level coverage (all proved by starting a host, not by reading source):
- StartupRefusesKeyRingSettingsWithNoRegisteredProvider
- StartupRefusesARegisteredProviderWithNoExplicitRepository
- StartupRefusesADeveloperFileSystemKeyRing (approved encryptor left in place,
  so the repository is the only thing the case can fail on)
- StartupRefusesAnApprovedRepositoryWithNoEncryptor
- StartupAcceptsTheApprovedDurableKeyRingOutsideDevelopment
- DevelopmentIsNotSubjectToTheKeyRingRequirement (starts AND serves both
  constant routes with no key ring at all)
- EveryRejectedComponentIsDeclaredInTheFrameworkAssembly (proves the assembly
  rule covers each type name B-6 enumerates)
- TheApprovedTestProviderIsNotDeclaredInTheFrameworkAssembly (proves the
  acceptance cases are not passing for the wrong reason)

